WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.126 --> 00:00:03.211
The plane is stuck.

00:00:03.294 --> 00:00:05.005
It's a little stuck.

00:00:11.594 --> 00:00:14.514
-Wow.
-Wow. Oh, my God.

00:00:14.597 --> 00:00:16.766
-Holy shit.
-We're on an adventure.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:41.041
Welcome to the Maasai Mara.

00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:44.502
OK. Now it's sunny.

00:00:44.586 --> 00:00:47.839
And we're here, and it's so beautiful.

00:00:47.922 --> 00:00:49.007
I can't understand it.

00:00:52.594 --> 00:00:53.678
Zebra!

00:00:54.179 --> 00:00:56.431
Oh, I love that thing.

00:00:59.351 --> 00:01:01.686
I really never thought
I'd get a chance to come over here.

00:01:02.854 --> 00:01:05.482
You know, you see pictures,
and you never know actually,

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:08.735
what it really looks like
or how it really feels.

00:01:08.818 --> 00:01:11.363
And it just feels like
how it's supposed to be.

00:01:11.446 --> 00:01:12.906
Look, over there! Look, back, back!

00:01:12.989 --> 00:01:13.990
He's right there!

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:15.116
Like how it's been forever.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.951
Oh, my God! Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

00:01:19.704 --> 00:01:22.207
I'm so sorry. Sorry, sorry.

00:01:23.833 --> 00:01:26.127
I've never seen an elephant in real life.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:30.465
There's four!

00:01:33.635 --> 00:01:35.512
A baby!

00:01:41.893 --> 00:01:43.144
Oh, my gosh.

00:01:44.396 --> 00:01:46.606
It keeps getting crazier!

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.948
I don't know if I've ever seen
anything so beautiful.

00:01:55.573 --> 00:01:56.783
This is insane.

00:01:59.703 --> 00:02:03.665
And apparently there was a lion
next to my room last night.

00:02:04.249 --> 00:02:06.626
Really rude,
didn't even come say hi to me.

00:02:11.881 --> 00:02:16.344
If she wants to, you are her breakfast.

00:02:19.848 --> 00:02:21.766
It's really interesting to see
a specialized predator

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:23.518
like a cheetah in this space.

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:27.313
You get a better understanding
of why they need this much space.

00:02:27.397 --> 00:02:32.068
Why they need such a vast,
expansive land to exist.

00:02:36.031 --> 00:02:39.617
So, we have to walk
in a single file line.

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:42.996
And if anything happens...

00:02:44.414 --> 00:02:45.790
you don't run.

00:02:49.794 --> 00:02:51.629
Look at that big one.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.007
Oh, my God.

00:02:54.799 --> 00:02:55.800
You OK?

00:03:03.058 --> 00:03:04.434
My hands are shaking.

00:03:07.437 --> 00:03:11.358
OK, I've been told
I have to calm down, so, I am.

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:14.194
I've now...
had a panic attack and cried.

00:03:14.277 --> 00:03:16.529
But I feel like I'm in
a better place now, right?

00:03:26.164 --> 00:03:27.123
You guys, it's happening.

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:46.184
I think I'll need
two gin and tonics tonight.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:52.315
Nine lions just passed by so close

00:03:52.399 --> 00:03:56.319
that my iPhone wouldn't
shoot on portrait mode.

00:03:56.403 --> 00:03:57.529
That's how close they were.

00:03:57.612 --> 00:03:58.613
Yep.

00:04:00.448 --> 00:04:01.741
Cheers.

00:04:03.994 --> 00:04:06.871
In my time here, the last three days,

00:04:06.955 --> 00:04:11.042
I have seen lots of elephants, giraffes

00:04:11.126 --> 00:04:14.629
baby... lions, zebras...

00:04:14.921 --> 00:04:17.549
Which I guess are pronounced zeb-ras.
Who knew?

00:04:17.632 --> 00:04:19.968
I have seen a lot more

00:04:20.051 --> 00:04:22.178
than I ever thought
I'd see in my whole life.

00:04:24.055 --> 00:04:26.016
And to me, what struck me the most,

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:30.979
is how beautiful and big this land is.

00:04:31.062 --> 00:04:32.647
And how fragile it is.

00:04:34.899 --> 00:04:37.027
It's just spectacular.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:40.238
The people... are spectacular.

00:04:40.322 --> 00:04:42.490
The culture is spectacular,

00:04:42.574 --> 00:04:44.409
the animals are, of course, spectacular.

00:04:44.492 --> 00:04:46.077
She's so beautiful.

00:04:46.161 --> 00:04:48.788
There is a future and hope for

00:04:48.872 --> 00:04:53.126
a world in which animals, wildlife,
humans, can coexist peacefully.

00:04:53.209 --> 00:04:56.212
Oh, they're so amazing.

00:04:56.296 --> 00:04:58.757
But being here and seeing first-hand,

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:00.175
it becomes that much more clear

00:05:00.258 --> 00:05:04.721
that if we continue
to care and love and nurture...

00:05:06.431 --> 00:05:07.557
there is hope.

00:05:08.558 --> 00:05:10.477
We just have to stay on that path.

